h contain the terms $1$ and $2$.","$(1,1,2)$ has two terms, since the repeated $1$ counts once.","$\\{1,2\\}\\ne\\{2,1\\}$, since the order of listing matters."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"91f94fa3f29a9094df429058","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_finite_sequence_5e26389d_010_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"What is the last term of the finite sequence $(a_i)_{i=1}^{4}=(3,8,5,1)$?","options":["$1$","$8$","$4$","$3$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"eaf6ede0335696a61c068cec","time_limit":20},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_finite_sequence_5e26389d_012_curated20261027_004","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"The finite sequence $(a_i)_{i=1}^{3}=(5,8,8)$ is viewed as a function $a$ with $a(i)=a_i$. Which statement is correct?","options":["Its domain is $\\{1,2,3\\}$, and $a(2)=a(3)=8$.","It is not a function, since the value $8$ occurs twice.","Its domain is $\\{5,8\\}$, the set of its values.","Its domain is $\\mathbb{N}$, as for every sequence."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b356922f908f0682dbd5d127","time_limit":35},{"id":"finite_sequence_expansion_004_curated20261027_005","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"How many terms does the finite sequence $(a_i)_{i=-2}^{3}$ have?","options":["$6$","$5$","$3$","$4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3f1df8740750d7117269f4db","time_limit":30},{"id":"finite_sequence_expansion_008_curated20261027_006","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"For $a_i=i^2$ with $i=0,1,2,3$, which finite sequence is obtained?","options":["$(1,2,3,4)$","$(0,2,4,6)$","$(1,4,9,16)$","$(0,1,4,9)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"b6ccc174bb8cc653da29c3bc","time_limit":20}]}}